    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23904" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sŏnus</span></b> 
		a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>without sound</i>, <i>noiseless</i>, <i>silent</i> (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">passus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 12</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gressus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 29, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestigium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 138, 22</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: litterae, i. e. mutae, App. de
